/-!
# VIII08 — the horizon compactification `Ac(x) = x · Y(1/x)` and its real limit `A0`

On the physical range `x ∈ (0, 1/3]` we have `Ac x = aY (1/x)`, so all bounds follow from the
proved monotone sandwich for `aY`.  `aY` is monotone on `(3, ∞)` and bounded above by `27/16`;
hence the limit `A0 = sSup (aY '' Ioi 3)` exists and `A0 ∈ [1/3, 27/16]`.  `Ac 0` is then *defined*
by this limit (not assumed to be differentiable there).
-/

set_option maxHeartbeats 2000000

open Set Filter Topology MeasureTheory intervalIntegral

namespace ExactVacuumAtlas.EinsteinMaxwell.ES5.KerrSchild.VIII08

open ExactVacuumAtlas ExactVacuumAtlas.EinsteinMaxwell ExactVacuumAtlas.EinsteinMaxwell.D
open ExactVacuumAtlas.EinsteinMaxwell.ES5
open ExactVacuumAtlas.EinsteinMaxwell.ES5.KerrSchild.Radial
open ExactVacuumAtlas.EinsteinMaxwell.ES5.KerrSchild.VIII04

/-! ## `Ac` and its identification with `aY ∘ (1/·)` -/

/-- `Ac x = x · Y(1/x)`.  Total on `ℝ`; only `x ∈ (0, 1/3]` is used. -/
noncomputable def Ac (x : ℝ) : ℝ := x * Y (1 / x)

/-! ## The limit `A0` -/

/-- The real limit `A0 = lim_{R→∞} aY R = lim_{x→0⁺} Ac x`. -/
noncomputable def A0 : ℝ := sSup (aY '' Ioi (3:ℝ))

/-! ## `aY` at and beyond the horizon -/

/-! ## The compactification on `K` -/

/-- `AcK` is `Ac` with the value `A0` filled in at `0`. -/
noncomputable def AcK (x : ℝ) : ℝ := if x = 0 then A0 else Ac x

/-! ## Continuity of `AcK` on `K` -/

end ExactVacuumAtlas.EinsteinMaxwell.ES5.KerrSchild.VIII08


